n't used everywhere. Use it  everywhere, including in CreateHttpConn.  -Support wildcard cookies in our little cookie jar monkeypatch.  -Fetch the commit-msg hook from a public location, rather than having  to deal with authentication in yet another context. This hook has  been very stable over the many years of Gerrit's existence.  Change-Id: Idbbd8ab4b4dcfc9fa27710d5abd4238b153b863e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357963 Commit-Ready: Dave Borowitz &lt;dborowitz@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dave Borowitz &lt;dborowitz@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Jonathan Nieder &lt;jrn@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="357963" owner_email="dborowitz@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/63/357963/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibae1836cb569fe89dd2c8249f76c66b78b1c2cf4" commit="950a921bdd34172d6ac1b395f7801954424d30c3" commit_message="bdb: Add nvmrw_get and nvmrw_set  These internal APIs are used to get and set values in NVM-RW variables.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51907 BRANCH=tot TEST=make runtests  Change-Id: Ibae1836cb569fe89dd2c8249f76c66b78b1c2cf4 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356691 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356691" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/91/356691/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icac23cc37029ac49c0df1d33c423dce1990ee319" commit="6fb06bdecd9808f66ded25ae130f118a18de43e0" commit_message="Increase test timeout allowances for canaries.  This increases the test timeouts allowed for canary builds.  The lab is suffering ongoing problems with aborts during canary testing, due the number of tests.  With the splitting of all canaries into single builders, we now have more headroom for test time, so let's use it.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Icac23cc37029ac49c0df1d33c423dce1990ee319 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358968 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358968" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/68/358968/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia72620316d7d0c67cd529c6effe66ebce8dce1b9" commit="cd14ccdeb531eae2ac6f95ccc52354d884ca9b94" commit_message="libcontainer_overrides: initial revision  This is a preload library for custom generic containers. For now, can talk to broker_service outside the container, and it just implements open and open64. Based off initial code by ksanthanam@.  BUG=chromium:622796 TEST=emerge-cyan libpreload with ebuild produces preload.so Change-Id: Ia72620316d7d0c67cd529c6effe66ebce8dce1b9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/355710 Commit-Ready: Ashish Gaurav &lt;ashishgaurav@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ashish Gaurav &lt;ashishgaurav@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="355710" owner_email="ashishgaurav@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/10/355710/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If3927460d12c4742793924a4ae5